{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F9fXmXzaYXobfymuVBUveV","type":"tool_result","content":"commit 3dfe597ff8c90c5d58e06ab84a245c14f51d4d26\nAuthor: Philip Reese <philipreese@mail.com>\nDate:   Tue Sep 1 22:41:45 2026 -0400\n\n    fix(flow): Clamp far-future exhaustion park delays and pace stale ones\n    \n    Task.Delay on a multi-year vendor reset instant crashed the pump with\n    ArgumentOutOfRangeException, and a reset instant already in the past\n    collapsed to a zero-delay retry that could machine-gun a still-exhausted\n    quota. Caps GetRetryObligations to a 14-day horizon (keeping RetryNotBefore\n    and RetryDelayMs mutually consistent for DependencyResolver's #712 clamp),\n    paces a past-or-imminent instant to a 1s floor, and chunks both park waits\n    into <=1-day Task.Delay calls so a capped-but-still-long wait never exceeds\n    the TimeSpan overload's ~49.7-day ceiling.\n\n src/Baton/Mutation/MutationInterface.cs            |  61 ++++-\n .../Mutation/MutationInterfaceRetryBackoffTests.cs | 252 ++++++++++++++++++++-\n 2 files changed, 306 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)\n===\ncommit 6e0f48bb4742374bce37e9c1fa37529ff888188e\nAuthor: Philip Reese <philipreese@mail.com>\nDate:   Tue Sep 1 23:53:12 2026 -0400\n\n    fix(flow): Dedupe quota-park notice on the raw instant, not the paced one\n    \n    Second-reader review of the #1183 fix found the past-instant floor\n    recomputing a fresh now+1s obligation on every retry of a repeating stale\n    instant, so deduping the #1094 park notice on that paced value re-notified\n    (and re-dispatched) once a second forever instead of once per distinct\n    vendor refusal. Dedupe on the raw vendor-reported instant instead, round\n    delayMs up rather than to nearest so the #712 clamp can never misfire on a\n    sub-millisecond rounddown, add a positive assertion to the far-future pump\n    test, and correct spec/baton.md and WorkflowStatusView's doc comment, both\n    of which still described exhaustedUntil as always the untouched vendor value.\n\n spec/baton.md                                      | 13 +++++++--\n src/Baton/Mutation/MutationInterface.cs            | 32 +++++++++++++++-------\n src/Baton/Status/WorkflowStatusView.cs             |  9 ++++--\n .../Mutation/MutationInterfaceRetryBackoffTests.cs | 15 +++++++---\n 4 files changed, 49 insertions(+), 20 deletions(-)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0cf3ee6d-fad8-4281-88ce-0dc9b70d8f50","uuid":"eee59254-d390-4209-9421-1510f4c6fe0a","timestamp":"2026-09-02T03:59:22.385Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"commit 3dfe597ff8c90c5d58e06ab84a245c14f51d4d26\nAuthor: Philip Reese <philipreese@mail.com>\nDate:   Tue Sep 1 22:41:45 2026 -0400\n\n    fix(flow): Clamp far-future exhaustion park delays and pace stale ones\n    \n    Task.Delay on a multi-year vendor reset instant crashed the pump with\n    ArgumentOutOfRangeException, and a reset instant already in the past\n    collapsed to a zero-delay retry that could machine-gun a still-exhausted\n    quota. Caps GetRetryObligations to a 14-day horizon (keeping RetryNotBefore\n    and RetryDelayMs mutually consistent for DependencyResolver's #712 clamp),\n    paces a past-or-imminent instant to a 1s floor, and chunks both park waits\n    into <=1-day Task.Delay calls so a capped-but-still-long wait never exceeds\n    the TimeSpan overload's ~49.7-day ceiling.\n\n src/Baton/Mutation/MutationInterface.cs            |  61 ++++-\n .../Mutation/MutationInterfaceRetryBackoffTests.cs | 252 ++++++++++++++++++++-\n 2 files changed, 306 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)\n===\ncommit 6e0f48bb4742374bce37e9c1fa37529ff888188e\nAuthor: Philip Reese <philipreese@mail.com>\nDate:   Tue Sep 1 23:53:12 2026 -0400\n\n    fix(flow): Dedupe quota-park notice on the raw instant, not the paced one\n    \n    Second-reader review of the #1183 fix found the past-instant floor\n    recomputing a fresh now+1s obligation on every retry of